x_comment(x_deadPhysicalRemains,"A binary predicate that relates a given type of living thing (see #$BiologicalLivingObject) to the type of dead physical remains of such things.  <code>(#$deadPhysicalRemains BLO-TYPE REMAINS-TYPE)</code> means that <code>REMAINS-TYPE</code> is the collection of all instances of #$OrganicMaterial that are the dead physical remains of an instance of <code>BLO-TYPE</code>.  For example, this predicate relates #$Hamster to the collection of all hamster corpses, i.e. hamster bodies (still recognizable as such) that are no longer alive.  Note that once a dead hamster's body has decayed to the point where it is no longer recognizable as a hamster's body, it is no longer a hamster corpse.\n<p>\nSee also the corresponding function #$DeadPhysicalRemainsFn.  And see this predicate's instance level correlate #$deadPhysicalRemainsOf.") :- x_cid(a65b126f7c9f54).
xc_microtheory(a65b126f7c9f54,x_BiologyMt).
